  "pacific_island": 1,
  "california_native": 0,
  "ethnobotanical_info": "This stunning tree is native to Argentina and Bolivia, but is now cultivated throughout the tropical world for its dramatic seasonal display of purple flowers. Used in South American traditional medicine to treat cold symptoms, rheumatism, wounds, and venereal disease. The beauty of the Jacaranda tree has inspired a variety of contemporary non-traditional myths and stories across its non-native distribution. (Gachet & Schühly, 2009)",
  "pi_invasive": 0,
  "invasive_text": "",
  "ca_invasive": 0,
  "schoolyard": 1,
  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has delicate, fern-like leaves that provide a great opportunity to discuss compound leaf structures. Its vibrant, tubular flowers bloom in clusters, adding a splash of color to lessons on pollination and plant reproduction. The tree&#x27;s seed pods are woody and can be used to explore seed dispersal methods. Its seasonal flowering cycle can also serve as a practical example of phenology in urban environments.",
